  "implementation": [
    "Distinct enemy Order unit targets across locations, with combined current Might at most five. Zero targets are legal and no arbitrary target-count cap is imposed.",
    "At resolution, recheck target identities, current allegiance/domain and prohibitions. If the collective limit is exceeded, the controller chooses an inclusion-maximal subset of original eligible targets, including every zero-Might target.",
    "The same explicit subset action and validator serve the native board, card-art tray, bot API and built-in AI; bounded bot suggestions do not enumerate every legal subset.",
    "Native controls show current Might and the remaining group budget. Confirm remains unavailable while another original eligible target still fits.",
    "Both nonblocking companion levels explain the limit and how opposing responses can change it.",
    "Reusable native and API baseline runners consume release-plan cases; full records and previous results are preserved for review."
  ],
